// near-zero half-ULP tie: x = +/-10^-(S/2) puts the second-order term of expm1(x) = x + x^2/2 + x^3/6 + ... at EXACTLY half an ULP past the grid point x at scale S (x^2/2 = (1/2)*10^-S), so the round is decided only by x^3/6 at depth 3S/2+1 - S/2 digits below the kernel's SCALE+GUARD, forcing the Ziv escalation. A kernel that stops at the guard sees ...5000 and applies the exact-tie rule, which is wrong in a different mode per sign: HalfToEven mis-rounds the positive row (last digit even, so the tie rule holds it down), HalfTowardZero the negative one. Series arm - |x| <= 1 at every cell, so these rows are evidence about expm1_series, not expm1_via_exp. One pair per even golden scale S <= 820, above which the deciding term falls past the oracle's stored 1233 digits and the value would read as a tie it is not
