// Trunc non-commutation, power-of-ten argument: x = -10^-m. Trunc rounds toward ZERO, and expm1(x) < 0 while exp(x) in (0,1) is positive, so the two forms round the SAME residual in OPPOSITE directions - Trunc(exp(x)) - 1 is the floor, Trunc(expm1(x)) the ceiling, one ULP apart whenever the residual is nonzero (the nearest and directed modes all commute, because expm1 and exp differ by exactly 1, an exact multiple of the ULP; only the sign-dependent modes do not). Here expm1(-10^-m) = -10^-m + (1/2)*10^-2m sits strictly between the grid points -10^-m and 0 at S = m, so the correct Trunc answer is exactly 0 while a composed exp-minus-one returns -10^-m - the starkest form of the split, and the reason expm1 exists as its own function rather than a composition. HalfTowardZero splits the same way at a tie. NO oracle-depth bound applies: non-exactness is carried by the 9-run immediately below the LSB, not by a deep deciding digit, so m runs EVERY golden scale, D18 through D1232's 1231. Series arm. Arguments already listed above as tie arguments are not repeated; the split applies to them at S = m just the same
